{"abstract":"Based on ethnographic observations of hospital video consultations between clinicians and patients, this article investigates the shifting places of care when consultations are displaced from the clinic. While information and communication technologies allow care across distance, scholars within science and technology studies (STS) and sociology have demonstrated how places still matter to the delivery of healthcare services. However, as healthcare increasingly enters the digital realm, we need a vo-cabulary and analytics which also address virtual environments' constitutive effects as places of care. This article argues that place must be understood as more than the locations of the consulting parties and be expanded to include the virtual places created during video consultations. Drawing on insights from STS and computer-supported cooperative work, the concept of hybrid place is proposed to capture the spatial hybridity of video consultations when physical locations are virtually connected and projected into virtual environments. The concept becomes a useful heuristic for understanding the spatial reconfiguration of the place of care during video consultations; it brings attention to the multiplicity of places, their connections and their distinct conditions which co-shape the virtual clinical encounter.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818235"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digitalisation","Healthcare","Outpatient clinics","Video consultations","Virtual care"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"when the place of care is hybrid an ethnographic study of hospital video consultations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/share/author/KQ3RFP3S5PGAB2PWBP25?target=10.1111/1467-9566.70053","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding provided by the Velux Foundation under Grant 26584, and the IT University of Copenhagen."],"id":"S01-000.00-818235","identifier":[{"id":"105007532548","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-282a2112-69e0-4bd0-ab78-0f0f8f6d59cf"],"keyword":["Digitalisation","Healthcare","Outpatient clinics","Video consultations","Virtual care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-02371403AB7BFE562A0F4FE4DF65468A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/share/author/KQ3RFP3S5PGAB2PWBP25?target=10.1111/1467-9566.70053","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie Sloth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"3ef9211c-34b2-4061-ba59-c5800d6a5b32","name":"Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","orcid":"0000-0001-7102-7268","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1467-9566.70053","issn":["01419889","14679566"],"issn_org":["01419889"],"issue":"5","journal":"Sociology of Health and Illness","pages":"1-30","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Sociology of Health and Illness","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007532548"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-282a2112-69e0-4bd0-ab78-0f0f8f6d59cf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"When the Place of Care Is Hybrid: An Ethnographic Study of Hospital Video Consultations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818235","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Whilst STS has long studied lab work, the past few years have also seen the introduction of labs as social formations for doing STS enquiry. But what kind of contributions to pedagogy, particularly in technical universities, can STS inspired university labs make? We respond to the need to more deeply understand how teaching may be practiced as a site of STS experimentation by describing the work of the ETHOS Lab, our critical feminist lab at the IT University of Copenhagen, as ‘enlivening’. Using three events from 2017–2020 as case studies, we identify both the use of space and shaping of time as integral to how we have sought to trouble knowledge production in our own environment, particularly by creating sites and situations where teaching and research cannot be separated. By showing how our Lab activities intervene in ways of knowing and doing within university hierarchies and cultures, we aim to contribute an analysis of the critical potential of STS lab work in technical environments, and recommendations from our situated evolving space of feminist praxis within an interdisciplinary IT University.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Cakici, Baki","Cohn, Marisa","Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Ojala, Mace","Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789556"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ruhr University Bochum"],"keyword":["Computer Science","Feminist pedagogy","LAB","Placemaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spaceships and poetry enlivening the lab as a site of feminist critical pedagogy","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17351/ests2023.1915","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789556","ids":["itu-711e4444-5f30-43d1-96a7-2c354602ea71"],"keyword":["computer science","feminist pedagogy","lab","placemaking","timework"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C15951B8EA8B501240253FD3148DCFAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17351/ests2023.1915","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://estsjournal.org/index.php/ests/article/view/1915/815","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ruhr university bochum","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ruhr University Bochum","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mace","key":"ojalapau","last":"Ojala","name":"Ojala, Mace","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie Sloth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"3ef9211c-34b2-4061-ba59-c5800d6a5b32","name":"Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","orcid":"0000-0001-7102-7268","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17351/ests2023.1915","issn":["24138053"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Engaging Science, Technology, and Society","publisher":"Society for Social Studies of Science","status":"p","title":"Engaging Science, Technology, and Society","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-711e4444-5f30-43d1-96a7-2c354602ea71"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spaceships and Poetry : Enlivening the Lab as a site of Feminist Critical Pedagogy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789556","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denne undersøgelse undersøger, hvordan unge arbejdstagere oplever ansættelsesforhold og ansvar for arbejdsmiljø i platformsøkonomien. Undersøgelsen er baseret på 29 kvalitative interviews med unge nordiske arbejdere (18-30 år), der finder arbejde gennem digitale arbejdsplatforme og sociale medieplatforme. Det Europæiske Arbejdsmiljøagentur hævder, at placeringen af ansvaret for arbejdsmiljøet i platformsøkonomien er udfordret af de uklare kategoriseringer af arbejdsgivere, arbejdstagere og selvstændige, og at den eksisterende arbejdsret og arbejdsmiljølovgivning kan være uanvendelig. Selv om de fleste platforme positionerer arbejdstagere som selvstændige, viser undersøgelsen, at de unge arbejdstagere sjældent oplever sig selv som selvstændige og antager, at platformene tager sig af arbejdsmiljøet. Når de unge arbejdstagere opererer i denne gråzone, risikerer de at stå uden beskyttelse og samfundsmæssige ressourcer til at forbedre deres arbejdsmiljø. Rasmussens model \"migration mod grænsen for uacceptabel sikkerhedsresultater\" bruges til at diskutere, hvordan arbejdsaktiviteter i platformsarbejde er drevet af stærke omkostnings- og indsatsforløb, mens modgradienten i form af arbejdsmiljøsystemer samtidig er meget svag eller helt fraværende.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mette Lykke","Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","Dyreborg, Johnny"],"cuid":["S02-089.82-767098"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Arbejdsmiljø","Digital platforms","Digitale platforme","Employment relations","Forebyggelse","Gig economy","M","Platformsøkonomi","Prevention","Sikkerhed","Unge"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"who takes care of safety and health among young workers responsibilization of osh in the platform economy","src":["aau","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssci.2022.105674","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.82-767098","identifier":[{"id":"85123612354","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e48a5bf7-8d35-4a9c-9299-67e9ca5ba9cf","nfa-4e86b4ea-4332-45de-9859-8c462ae6905a"],"keyword":["Digital platforms","Digitale platforme","Employment relations","M","Migration toward accidents","Platformsøkonomi","Prevention","Protective gaps","Unge","arbejdsmiljø","beskæftigelsesrelationer","forbyggelse","forebyggelse","gig economy","sikkerhed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E297C1417A3302DEF0C8F65938DB1F59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssci.2022.105674","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, Centre for Youth Research (CeFU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Psychosocial Working Environment and Working Accidents and Safety Culture"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Lykke","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"33131688-dbd7-457e-85aa-0229ea2c05f4","name":"Nielsen, Mette Lykke","orcid":"0000-0001-8834-9159","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie Sloth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnny","key":"dyreborgpau","last":"Dyreborg","locid":"d5a5dec6-836b-49e6-9044-bd0786cea744","name":"Dyreborg, J","name_org":"Dyreborg, Johnny","orcid":"0000-0002-5452-5596","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ssci.2022.105674","issn":["09257535"],"issue":"May","journal":"Safety Science","paperid":"105674","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Safety Science","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123612354"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e48a5bf7-8d35-4a9c-9299-67e9ca5ba9cf","nfa-4e86b4ea-4332-45de-9859-8c462ae6905a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Who takes care of safety and health among young workers? : Responsibilization of OSH in the platform economy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.82-767098","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"I 2021 trak arbejdsmiljøet hos Nemlig.com store overskrifter. Det skete parallelt med, at EU-Kommissionen satte fokus på beskæftigelsesforhold og regulering af digitale arbejdsplatforme. Samtidig rettede den danske regering opmærksomheden mod de ”gråzoner”, som præger platformsøkonomien, og beskæftigelsesministeren fastslog, at der måtte være ”ordnede forhold” på alle dele af det danske arbejdsmarked. Platformsøkonomien medvirker dermed til, at der stilles spørgsmål til indretningen af arbejdsmarkedet og regulering af atypisk beskæftigelse, herunder hvem der skal have ansvar for arbejdsmiljøet i platformsøkonomien i Danmark og på EU-niveau. På baggrund af dette sætter artiklen fokus på unge, der finder beskæftigelse på- og via digitale arbejdsplatforme. Den undersøger, hvordan de unge selv forstår og forholder sig til deres beskæftigelsesforhold, og mere specifikt til deres arbejdsmiljø. Med udgangspunkt i dette diskuteres placeringen af ansvaret for platformarbejderes arbejdsmiljø. Undersøgelsen er baseret på 14 kvalitative interviews med 18-30-årige unge. Desuden analyseres de udvalgte arbejdsplatformes egne online dokumenter om vilkår og betingelser. I analysen af materialet anvendes Rasmussens klassiske risikomodel ”drift to danger model” (Rasmussen, 1997). Artiklen viser, at selvom de fleste digitale arbejdsplatforme betragter og behandler platformsarbejderne som selvstændige, så opfatter de unge platformsarbejdere sjældent sig selv som selvstændige, og de tror ofte, at platformene tager ansvaret for deres arbejdsmiljø. Artiklen viser, at de unge platformsarbejderne befinder sig i en gråzone mellem selvstændig og ansat. Det betyder, at der er en risiko for, at arbejdsmiljøproblemer blandt unge platformsarbejdere ikke bliver forebygget, dels fordi det er uklart, hvem der har ansvaret for at håndtere disse, eller fordi organisering af arbejdsmiljøet og forebyggelseskulturen står svagt eller er helt fraværende.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mette Lykke","Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","Nielsen,, Louise Yung","Dyreborg, Johnny"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-767166"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["App","Arbejdsmiljø","Digitalisering","Platformsarbejde","Unge"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Center for Ungdomsforskning"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"når din leder er en app hvem har ansvaret for unges arbejdsmiljø i platformsøkonomien","src":["aau","nfa","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/tfa.v24i3.134745","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-767166","ids":["aau-fd449442-d0c0-44e0-9efb-8d38abab1966","nfa-51f7d3d8-2c91-4102-9367-dce4ff5f1f7b","ruc-b7a8c471-5392-4b26-892d-be020454cac0"],"keyword":["App","Arbejdsmiljø","Digitalisering","Platformsarbejde","Unge"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-958F8BBB8690951CC402BE9EA3310A4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/104221676/TfA_03_2022_INDMAD_OK_2185_split_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/tidsskrift-for-arbejdsliv/article/view/134745","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/tidsskrift-for-arbejdsliv/article/view/134745/179580","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/86199053/ML_Nielsen_mfl_Na_r_din_leder_er_en_app.pdf","versi